# rhyremix 60 fps profile - s22. Install with: tools/rtxprofile.sh perf [GAME_DIR]
#
# Generated from the live <game>/rtx.conf on 2026-11-11 (see .strata/notes-s22-60fps-budget.md
# for the evidence: every key here is in the runtime's own strings, checked with
# tools/rtxkeycheck.py --keys config/rtx-runtime-keys.txt config/rtx.conf.perf).
#
# What this file is for: MangoHud says ~60 fps with drops on a 4070 Ti SUPER 16 GB at 1080p.
# Tier A below is applied and is meant to buy headroom without changing the look of the pack.
# Tier B is commented: one line at a time, in the order given, re-testing between each.
#
# Two keys the shipped rtx.conf carries are NOT in this build of the runtime at all
# (`grep -c` on .trex/d3d9.dll and every other .trex module returns 0):
#   rtx.enableVolumetricLighting      -> replaced by rtx.volumetrics.enable (same switch, the
#                                        name this runtime has; the tooltip: "Enabling volumetric
#                                        lighting provides higher quality ray traced physical
#                                        volumetrics, disabling falls back to cheaper depth based
#                                        fog.")
#   rtx.minReplacementTextureMipMapLevel -> dropped; it was already a no-op here.
# Both are still in rtx.conf.orig / config/rtx.conf, so `tools/rtxprofile.sh current` puts them
# back.
#
# Read the runtime's own log after the first launch of a profile:
#   grep -A80 'Effective RtxOption values' <game>/rtx-remix/logs/remix-dxvk.log
# That dump is the only place the preset layers become visible (the last run showed
# rtx.neuralRadianceCache.trainingMaxPathBounces = 9, which no file in the game folder writes).

